---
pagination:
  data: pages.about.locales
  size: 1
  alias: locale
permalink: "{{ locale.permalink }}"
---
{#
  TAQATHON - ABOUT PAGE TEMPLATE (src/pages/about.njk)
  ------------------------------------------------------------
  Built as part of Phase 3's nav restructure — the new "About"
  dropdown in navbar.njk needed a real destination page, not just an
  empty menu label. Two stacked sections, association first then
  Taqathon itself, per explicit instruction — a simple content page,
  no forms/loops needed.

  REAL CONTENT (Phase 3, 2026 real-content pass): every body
  paragraph on this page is now sourced from the board-approved
  resolution for "طاقتون ٢" and taqa.org.sa — see about.ar.json /
  about.en.json's "_comment" field for the source of each. The
  "Official Status" sub-section was the one explicitly flagged as
  sensitive and not to be invented; it's now a confirmed fact (the
  Association's real license number), so it moved OUT of the dashed
  "pending confirmation" treatment (.ab-draft-flag, still defined
  below for any future placeholder that needs it) and into the plain
  "confirmed fact" callout (.ab-fact) — same solid-border pattern
  other pages in this redesign use for "here's a real, sourced note"
  (see community.njk's .ed-note), just under this page's own .ab-
  prefix instead of introducing a second shared class name.

  VISUAL SYSTEM (Phase 3, editorial redesign rollout — first page
  after Home): reuses the exact same tokens/mirror technique Home's
  hero/About sections established, not a new palette. Where this page
  differs from Home is intentional, not accidental:
    - Sections alternate cream → sky → cream → sky, same rhythm Home
      uses between its own sections, so navigating Home → About feels
      like the same site, not two different design systems.
    - Mission/Vision reuse Home's "two navy accent cards" pattern
      (.ab-pillar, mirrors Home's .dz-stat-cell) — text instead of a
      number, same idea: a small deliberate dark accent inside an
      otherwise light section.
    - Official Status gets a NEW pattern Home didn't need: a visibly
      flagged "draft, pending confirmation" callout (dashed terra
      border + mono label), because unlike Home's content, this
      section is explicitly not-yet-real information about a real
      organization, and the design should make that obvious to anyone
      reading the live site, not just to whoever reads this comment.
    - Dark mode: backgrounds flip for free (--color-cream/--color-sky
      are already redefined in common.css's dark block from Home's
      round 8). Text/accent overrides below follow the exact same
      rules Home's dark-mode block documents in full — amber takes
      over as the primary dark-mode accent, terra moves to the two
      small light-accent elements (the pillar cards), navy text
      becomes --text. See home.njk if the "why" here is unclear.
#}
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}
{% block pageHead %}
{# Same three fonts as Home, same reasoning: page-scoped so no other
   page pays for them until the redesign reaches it too. #}
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Big+Shoulders+Display:wght@600;700;800&family=Tajawal:wght@700;800;900&family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
{% endblock %}
{% block pageStyle %}
.ab-hero{ background:var(--color-cream); color:var(--brand-dark); padding:4rem 0 3rem; position:relative; overflow:hidden; border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.08); }
.ab-hero::before{
  content:""; position:absolute; top:-20%; inset-inline-end:-10%; width:420px; height:420px;
  background:radial-gradient(circle, rgba(196,64,26,.08), transparent 70%);
  border-radius:50%; pointer-events:none; z-index:0;
}
.ab-hero .container{ position:relative; z-index:1; max-width:760px; text-align:center; }
.ab-display{
  font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:700;
  font-size:clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem); line-height:1; letter-spacing:-.01em; margin:0;
}
[dir="rtl"] .ab-display{ font-family:'Tajawal', var(--font-display); font-weight:800; letter-spacing:0; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-hero{ color:var(--text); border-bottom-color:rgba(255,255,255,.08); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-hero::before{ background:radial-gradient(circle, rgba(232,149,43,.10), transparent 70%); }

{#
  Both content sections share one rule-set (.ab-section) since they're
  structurally identical (mono label + display heading + body copy) —
  only the background alternates, set per-section via a modifier
  class, same pattern as picking cream vs sky per section on Home.
#}
.ab-section{ padding:4rem 0; position:relative; }
.ab-section.tone-cream{ background:var(--color-cream); color:var(--brand-dark); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.08); }
.ab-section.tone-sky{ background:var(--color-sky); color:var(--brand-dark); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.08); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-section.tone-cream,
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-section.tone-sky{ color:var(--text); border-bottom-color:rgba(255,255,255,.08); }
.ab-section .container{ max-width:760px; }
.ab-label{
  font-family:var(--font-mono-label); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.08em;
  font-size:.75rem; color:var(--color-terra); margin-bottom:.6rem; display:block;
}
[dir="rtl"] .ab-label{ font-family:inherit; text-transform:none; letter-spacing:0; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-label{ color:var(--color-amber); }
.ab-heading{
  font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:1.25rem;
  font-size:clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); line-height:1.1; letter-spacing:-.01em;
}
[dir="rtl"] .ab-heading{ font-family:'Tajawal', var(--font-display); font-weight:800; letter-spacing:0; }
.ab-body{ color:var(--color-dust); max-width:56ch; margin-bottom:0; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-body{ color:var(--muted); }

{#
  Official Status: the one section on this page that's explicitly NOT
  ready to be treated as real content (see the front-matter comment
  and about.*.json's own flag). Previously this was a plain
  text-secondary paragraph under a border-top — easy to miss that
  it's a placeholder rather than finished copy. This makes it
  unmissable: a dashed terra border (terra already means "needs
  attention" elsewhere — the Home announcements' deadline-type icon),
  a small flag icon, and a mono "PENDING CONFIRMATION" label placed
  ABOVE the placeholder text itself, not buried after it.
#}
.ab-draft-flag{
  border:1.5px dashed rgba(196,64,26,.4); border-radius:.75rem;
  padding:1.25rem 1.5rem; margin-top:1.75rem; background:rgba(196,64,26,.04);
}
.ab-draft-flag-label{
  display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.5rem;
  font-family:var(--font-mono-label); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.06em;
  font-size:.7rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--color-terra); margin-bottom:.6rem;
}
[dir="rtl"] .ab-draft-flag-label{ font-family:inherit; text-transform:none; letter-spacing:0; }
.ab-draft-flag-body{ color:var(--color-dust); margin:0; font-size:.95rem; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-draft-flag{ border-color:rgba(232,149,43,.4); background:rgba(232,149,43,.06); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-draft-flag-label{ color:var(--color-amber); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-draft-flag-body{ color:var(--muted); }

{#
  .ab-fact: the "resolved" counterpart to .ab-draft-flag above — a
  SOLID terra border instead of dashed, no "pending" label, for a
  short factual note that's confirmed rather than awaiting
  confirmation. Currently used for Official Status now that its one
  real fact (the license number) is known.
#}
.ab-fact{
  border:1.5px solid rgba(196,64,26,.3); border-radius:.75rem;
  padding:1.25rem 1.5rem; margin-top:1.75rem; background:rgba(196,64,26,.04);
}
.ab-fact-label{
  display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.5rem;
  font-family:var(--font-mono-label); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.06em;
  font-size:.7rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--color-terra); margin-bottom:.6rem;
}
[dir="rtl"] .ab-fact-label{ font-family:inherit; text-transform:none; letter-spacing:0; }
.ab-fact-body{ color:var(--color-dust); margin:0; font-size:.95rem; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-fact{ border-color:rgba(232,149,43,.35); background:rgba(232,149,43,.06); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-fact-label{ color:var(--color-amber); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-fact-body{ color:var(--muted); }

{#
  Mission/Vision pillars: same small-dark-accent-in-a-light-section
  idea as Home's .dz-stat-cell, reused for text instead of a number.
  Dark mode flips them the same way too — light accent on a dark
  section, fixed cream (not the theme-flipping token) so they stay
  self-contained regardless of page theme, exactly like Home's cards.
#}
.ab-pillars{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px,1fr)); gap:1px; background:rgba(0,40,76,.1); border:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.1); border-radius:.75rem; overflow:hidden; margin-top:2rem; }
.ab-pillar{ background:var(--brand-dark); color:var(--color-cream); padding:1.5rem 1.75rem; }
.ab-pillar-label{ font-family:var(--font-mono-label); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.06em; font-size:.7rem; color:var(--color-mist); margin-bottom:.5rem; display:block; }
[dir="rtl"] .ab-pillar-label{ font-family:inherit; text-transform:none; letter-spacing:0; }
.ab-pillar-text{ margin:0; font-size:.95rem; line-height:1.5; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-pillar{ background:#FAF8F4; color:var(--brand-dark); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-pillar-label{ color:var(--color-dust); }

.ab-cta{ background:var(--color-sky); color:var(--color-dust); text-align:center; padding:4rem 0; position:relative; overflow:hidden; }
.ab-cta::before{
  content:""; position:absolute; bottom:-25%; inset-inline-start:-8%; width:360px; height:360px;
  background:radial-gradient(circle, rgba(232,149,43,.14), transparent 70%);
  border-radius:50%; pointer-events:none; z-index:0;
}
.ab-cta .container{ position:relative; z-index:1; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ab-cta{ color:var(--muted); }
.ab-cta-btn{ background:var(--color-amber); border:0; color:var(--brand-dark); font-weight:700; }
.ab-cta-btn:hover{ filter:brightness(1.05); color:var(--brand-dark); }
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<section class="ab-hero">
<div class="container">
  <h1 class="ab-display">{{ locale.content.taqathon.heading }}</h1>
</div>
</section>

<section class="ab-section tone-cream">
<div class="container">
  <span class="ab-label">01 — {{ locale.content.association.heading }}</span>
  <h2 class="ab-heading">{{ locale.content.association.heading }}</h2>
  <p class="ab-body">{{ locale.content.association.bodyPlaceholder }}</p>
  <div class="ab-fact">
    <div class="ab-fact-label"><i class="bi bi-patch-check-fill"></i> {{ locale.content.association.statusLabel }} — {{ locale.content.confirmedLabel }}</div>
    <p class="ab-fact-body">{{ locale.content.association.statusPlaceholder }}</p>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="ab-section tone-sky">
<div class="container">
  <span class="ab-label">02 — {{ locale.content.taqathon.heading }}</span>
  <h2 class="ab-heading">{{ locale.content.taqathon.heading }}</h2>
  <p class="ab-body">{{ locale.content.taqathon.bodyPlaceholder }}</p>
  <div class="ab-pillars">
    <div class="ab-pillar">
      <span class="ab-pillar-label">{{ locale.content.taqathon.missionHeading }}</span>
      <p class="ab-pillar-text">{{ locale.content.taqathon.missionPlaceholder }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ab-pillar">
      <span class="ab-pillar-label">{{ locale.content.taqathon.visionHeading }}</span>
      <p class="ab-pillar-text">{{ locale.content.taqathon.visionPlaceholder }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="ab-cta">
<div class="container">
  <p class="mb-3" style="font-size:1.05rem;">{{ locale.content.ctaLabel }}</p>
  <a class="btn ab-cta-btn px-4 py-2" href="{{ locale.content.ctaButtonHref }}">{{ locale.content.ctaButtonLabel }}</a>
</div>
</section>

{% endblock %}
